{"title":"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 3d","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a <i>Dlin sequence</i>, the first term is a positive integer and each term after the first is calculated by adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to the previous term in the sequence, then doubling the result. For example, the first seven terms of the Dlin sequence with first term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/b/0ab734f0d1d149f394bac30bed297bd11a88a924.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4, 10, 22, 46, 94, 190, 382$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"187\" height=\"17\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3d&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine the number of positive integers between 1 and 2020, inclusive, that can be the third term in a Dlin sequence.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3d&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd28b278a07bda0ea4d08737743613980c6aa6a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /><sup>th</sup> term of the Dlin sequence. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/9/199bbd4e91050883d9a86770d240cf2d3a85539d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> would then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/6/a065e6179aae0a4dfc1fed63ae4374804c475f84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(a_{1} + 1) = 2a_{1} + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"155\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/7/577f233ff970bde00137808bfa15c1e96df56f9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/2/ce20871042904bb2e566cdd627284c97625075aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(2a_{1} + 2 + 1) = 2(2a_{1} + 3) = 4a_{1} + 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"300\" height=\"20\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1da7198d9a79e0a6dc32e60162044ee0f726e4e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer, this must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/2/a12b29bee450db038013006a582d026d67b6bb82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$503 \\times 4 + 6 = 2018$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"152\" height=\"15\" /> but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/f/bbf7835bfc628a9a8c3890e789c65674dde6dfa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$504 \\times 4 + 6 = 2018 + 4 = 2022 &gt; 2020$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"305\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/b/82b06433bf3749ab1091dd79f50ddcb5cb99c8e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{503}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" /> possible values for the third term.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018012801\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.016 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 55/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 452/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2756/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.870      1 2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3\n100.00%    6.870      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36617:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018012801 and revision id 282465. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}